1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,510
A square with an area of 2 —
how long is each side?

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:06,430
A square made of 4 grid squares

3
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:09,000
Connect the middles of the four sides

4
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:12,670
What if we fold the 4 corners in?

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:15,840
They fill the inside exactly!
Inside = half of the whole

6
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:17,610
Half of 4 → an area of 2

7
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,780
So each side of this square is √2

8
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:27,350
√2 times √2 is 2.
Let's look for that number

9
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,800
It gets closer,
but never exactly 2

10
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:35,370
Its decimals go on forever: 1.41421356…

11
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:40,970
Multiplication is area — the end!
